== a national celebration
tier: read
source: institution
tone: joy
base: need:belonging+.15 need:meaning+.05
earth: a national holiday, a jubilee or a big anniversary: flags, parades and fireworks
times: once a year, with a big one every decade or two
window: 12-110
gap: 1-10
likelier: peace, a shared history, a round anniversary
rarer: a divided country, war, a person far from their own country
scene: Flags hang from every window, the high street is closed for the parade, and fireworks are promised at dusk.
- W | a day to honour the country and those who served it | impact: 1.2 | also: meaning+.05 | say: {N} stands for the anthem with a hand on the heart.
- U | a show worth understanding: who organised it, and why now | impact: 0.7 | say: {N} watches the parade with a guidebook, reading up on every regiment.
- B | a day off, crowds, and good business | impact: 0.9 | say: {N} sells flags from a folding table and does very well.
- R | fireworks, crowds, and a party in the street | impact: 1.2 | also: belonging+.05 | say: {N} is out in the street until the last rocket goes up.
- G | the old customs, kept alive one more year | impact: 0.9 | also: belonging+.05 | say: {N} goes to the same spot by the river where {grandparent} once watched.

== new people move in next door
