rarer: a settled village where nobody moves
scene: A removal van blocks the street all morning. By the afternoon a stranger is at {Ns} door with a tray of something homemade.
- W | welcome them properly, with a card and an offer of help | impact: 1.0 | say: {N} brings round a card and offers to show them where everything is.
- U | who are they, and where are they from? | impact: 0.9 | say: {N} asks a dozen questions on the doorstep and learns where they came from.
- B | a new face; find out what they do | impact: 0.8 | say: {N} learns within a week that the newcomer runs a building firm.
- R | a new friend, maybe; have them over tonight | impact: 1.2 | also: belonging+.05 | say: {N} is round there making friends before the boxes are even unpacked.
