- U | note the first swallow, the first blossom, and the date | impact: 0.9 | say: {N} writes the date of the first swallow in the notebook, as every year.
- B | the café terrace is open, and the best table is free | impact: 0.9 | also: autonomy+.05 | say: {N} takes the best table on the terrace before the lunch crowd.
- R | skip the afternoon and go to the lake | impact: 1.3 | also: autonomy+.05 | say: {N} slips away early and is in the lake by three.
- G | the year turns, as it always does | impact: 1.1 | also: meaning+.05 | say: {N} walks barefoot on the new grass and feels the ground waking.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- troubles

== a pandemic and a lockdown
tier: read
source: institution
tone: trouble
base: need:belonging-.3 need:safety-.25 need:autonomy-.2
earth: a new disease spreads and the country locks down: schools closed, streets empty, family visits forbidden
times: once or twice in a life
window: 12-110
gap: 30-80
likelier: a crowded, connected world; weak health systems; a person who lives alone
rarer: remote places; strong early action
scene: The streets are empty at noon. The schools are shut, the shops let people in a few at a time, and the only sound is an ambulance far away.
- W | follow the rules to the letter, and help others keep them | impact: 0.9 | also: meaning+.05 | say: {N} keeps a careful distance in every queue and shops for the old neighbour every week.
- U | read every study and track every number | impact: 1.0 | also: competence+.05 safety-.05 | say: {N} keeps a spreadsheet of the case numbers and checks it every morning.
- B | stock up early, and look after your own | impact: 0.9 | also: safety+.05 belonging-.05 | say: {N} stocks up in the first week and keeps a stash nobody else may touch.
- R | going mad indoors, climbing the walls | impact: 1.3 | also: autonomy-.05 | say: {N} paces the flat at night, then breaks the rules for a walk by the river.
- G | hard times come and go; keep close to home and wait it out | impact: 0.9 | also: belonging+.05 | say: {N} bakes bread, tends the window boxes and rings the family every evening.

== a recession
tier: read
source: institution
tone: trouble
base: need:safety-.25 need:competence-.1 res:money-.05
earth: the economy shrinks: firms close, prices rise, and everyone knows someone who lost a job
times: every eight to ten years
window: 14-110
gap: 6-12
likelier: a trade that follows the business cycle, debt, a one-industry town
rarer: a public-sector job, a pension, savings
scene: Half the shops on the high street have whitewashed windows, and the news talks of nothing but the downturn.
- W | tighten belts together; everyone must pull their weight | impact: 0.9 | also: belonging+.05 | say: {N} cuts back, and joins the food bank rota on Saturdays.
- U | it was predictable; read the signs for the next move | impact: 0.9 | also: competence+.05 | say: {N} studies the forecasts and works out what the household should cut first.
- B | bad times make a buyer's market | impact: 0.7 | also: autonomy+.05 | say: {N} buys cheap from people who have to sell.
- R | furious at the bankers, the bosses, all of them | impact: 1.2 | also: meaning-.05 | say: {N} shouts at the television and joins the march on Saturday.
- G | lean years follow fat years | impact: 0.9 | also: safety+.05 | say: {N} grows more vegetables and stops buying what the household can make.

== a disaster in the next town
tier: read
source: environment
tone: trouble
base: need:safety-.2 need:belonging-.1
