times: a few times in a life
window: 12-110
gap: 5-20
likelier: floodplains, fire country, storm coasts, a warming climate
rarer: sheltered inland places
scene: The river burst its banks in the night. Ten miles away a whole town is under muddy water, and {Ns} phone is full of messages from people who live there.
- W | organise: collect, sort, send, help | impact: 1.0 | also: meaning+.05 | say: {N} helps at the collection point in the school hall all week.
- U | why there, why now, and what would have stopped it? | impact: 0.8 | also: competence+.05 | say: {N} studies the flood maps and writes to the council about the defences.
- B | it could have been here; make sure your own are protected first | impact: 0.9 | also: safety+.05 | say: {N} packs an emergency bag that afternoon and checks the family is covered.
- R | get over there and start bailing | impact: 1.2 | also: belonging+.05 | say: {N} gets a lift over with a load of buckets and works until dark.
- G | the river takes back what was its own | impact: 1.1 | also: meaning-.05 | say: {N} stands on the bridge and watches the muddy water for a long time.

