- U | find out exactly what happened, and who knew | impact: 0.9 | also: competence+.05 | say: {N} reads every report and asks the hard questions at the meeting.
- B | everyone has a price; trust no one with power | impact: 0.8 | also: autonomy+.05 meaning-.05 | say: {N} stops putting money in the plate and keeps it.
- R | betrayed; walk out and never come back | impact: 1.2 | say: {N} storms out of the meeting and does not go back.
- G | people fall; the old faith remains | impact: 0.9 | also: meaning+.05 | say: {N} prays alone at home, as {grandparent} used to.

== break-ins on the street
tier: read
source: community
tone: trouble
base: need:safety-.25
earth: two houses on your street are burgled in one week, and everyone is checking their locks
times: a few times in a life
window: 12-110
gap: 2-10
likelier: cities, poverty nearby, hard times
rarer: small close villages
scene: A police car sits outside number twelve all morning. Their back door was forced in the night, the second break-in on the street this week.
- W | set up a neighbourhood watch and work with the police | impact: 1.0 | also: belonging+.05 | say: {N} helps get a neighbourhood watch going and keeps an eye out every evening.
- U | work out how they got in, and fix the weak points | impact: 0.8 | also: competence+.05 | say: {N} walks round the house testing every lock and window.
- B | better locks, cameras, and a big dog | impact: 0.9 | also: safety+.05 | say: {N} pushes for new locks and a camera, and checks them every night.
- R | furious; if they come here, they will regret it | impact: 1.2 | say: {N} sleeps with a cricket bat by the bed.
- G | keep close to the neighbours, and the street will mind itself | impact: 0.9 | also: belonging+.05 | say: {N} gets to know the old couple next door, and they keep an eye out for each other.

== a rumour about you
tier: read
source: community
tone: trouble
base: need:belonging-.25 need:safety-.05
earth: you hear that people at work, at school or in the street are saying something untrue about you
times: a few times in a life
window: 12-110
gap: 2-8
likelier: a small workplace or school, a rival, a public role
rarer: few ties, a big anonymous world
scene: {friend} stops talking when {N} walks in. Later {N} learns what is being said, and that it is not true.
- W | set the record straight, calmly, with the facts | impact: 1.0 | say: {N} goes to the people repeating it and corrects it, point by point.
- U | trace it to its source | impact: 0.9 | also: competence+.05 | say: {N} works out within a day who started it, and why.
- B | find who started it, and return the favour | impact: 1.1 | also: autonomy+.05 belonging-.05 | say: {N} lets slip a little something about the one who started it.
- R | hurt and fury; take it on head first | impact: 1.2 | also: autonomy+.05 | say: {N} marches up to the lunch table and dares whoever said it to say it again.
- G | people talk; let it blow over | impact: 0.8 | say: {N} shrugs it off and carries on as before.

== an insult from a stranger
tier: read
source: daily life
tone: trouble
base: need:belonging-.1 need:competence-.05
earth: a stranger in the street, the car park or online says something cruel about how you look, speak or live
times: a few times a year
window: 12-110
gap: 0.2-2
likelier: crowded cities, online life, standing out from the crowd
rarer: a small friendly place, a life mostly offline
scene: In the car park a man leans out of his window, shouts something ugly at {N}, and drives off laughing.
- W | rude and wrong; report it if it goes further | impact: 0.9 | say: {N} notes the number plate, just in case.
- U | what made them like that? | impact: 0.7 | also: competence+.05 | say: {N} turns it over on the way home, wondering what makes a person say that.
- B | it says more about them than about you | impact: 0.8 | also: autonomy+.05 | say: {N} shrugs and decides the man is not worth a second thought.
- R | a slap in the face; the anger burns all day | impact: 1.3 | say: {N} shouts after the car, and is still shaking an hour later.
- G | a sour wind; it will blow past | impact: 0.7 | also: meaning+.05 | say: {N} takes a breath, looks at the sky, and lets it go.

== a bill you did not expect
tier: read
source: daily life
tone: trouble
base: need:safety-.15 res:money-.05
earth: the boiler breaks, the car fails its test, or a tax demand arrives, and it is more than you have
times: once or twice a year
window: 18-110
gap: 0.3-2
likelier: an old house or car, no savings, a tight budget
rarer: savings, new things, a landlord who pays
scene: The mechanic wipes his hands and names a figure. It is three times what {N} has in the bank.
- W | pay it, cut back, and set up a fund for next time | impact: 0.9 | also: competence+.05 | say: {N} pays it in instalments and opens a rainy-day account the same week.
- U | check every line; there may be a mistake | impact: 0.8 | also: competence+.05 | say: {N} finds two errors on the bill and gets it reduced.
- B | haggle hard, or find someone who will do it cheaper | impact: 1.0 | also: autonomy+.05 | say: {N} gets three quotes and beats the price down by a third.
- R | why now, of all times? | impact: 1.2 | say: {N} kicks the tyre, swears, and puts it on the credit card.
- G | things wear out; it was their time | impact: 0.8 | also: meaning+.05 | say: {N} sighs, borrows from {sibling}, and mends what can be mended.

== a heatwave
tier: read
source: environment
tone: trouble
base: need:safety-.15 need:autonomy-.05
earth: weeks of record heat: sleepless nights, burnt lawns, warnings for the old and the sick
times: most summers now, a severe one every few years
window: 12-110
gap: 1-5
likelier: a warming climate, cities, old age, poor housing
rarer: cool coastal places
scene: The thermometer on the shed reads forty in the shade. The tarmac is soft, the lawns are brown, and nobody has slept properly in a week.
- W | check on the old and frail, and keep to the water rules | impact: 0.9 | also: belonging+.05 | say: {N} knocks on the old neighbours' doors each afternoon with bottles of water.
- U | understand it: the climate, the records, what is coming | impact: 0.9 | also: meaning-.05 | say: {N} reads the climate reports late into the hot night.
- B | keep cool, and never mind the cost | impact: 0.7 | also: safety+.05 | say: {N} grabs the last fan in the shop and keeps it in {Ns} own room.
- R | heat in the blood: short tempers and long nights | impact: 1.2 | also: autonomy+.05 | say: {N} snaps at everyone by day and swims in the river after dark.
- G | the land is suffering; slow down with it | impact: 1.0 | also: meaning-.05 | say: {N} closes the shutters at dawn and lives slowly, the way people do in hot countries.

== a run of bad luck
tier: read
source: cosmology
tone: trouble
base: need:safety-.1 need:meaning-.1 need:competence-.05
earth: in one week the car breaks down, the phone is lost and a pipe bursts, and it starts to feel personal
times: a few times a year
window: 12-110
gap: 0.2-2
likelier: hard times, old things, stress
rarer: calm, well-kept lives
scene: Monday the car, Wednesday the phone, Friday a pipe bursts under the kitchen sink. By Saturday {N} half expects the roof to fall in.
- W | a test of patience; keep steady and do what must be done | impact: 0.9 | also: meaning+.05 | say: {N} deals with each thing in order and refuses to complain.
- U | coincidence; there is no such thing as a curse | impact: 0.7 | also: competence+.05 | say: {N} works out the odds on the back of an envelope and laughs at them.
- B | someone or something is behind this | impact: 1.0 | also: safety-.05 | say: {N} goes over the week, looking for whoever could be to blame.
- R | the world is laughing; laugh back, or kick something | impact: 1.2 | also: autonomy+.05 | say: {N} kicks the bucket under the sink, then laughs until it hurts.
- G | a bad season; keep low until it passes | impact: 1.0 | also: meaning+.05 | say: {N} keeps to the house for the weekend and waits for the turn.
